  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "20342237",
      "title": "Repeating the Example with Node",
      "lectureOrder": 523,
      "videoOrder": 464,
      "sourceHash": "626ef55256f17e74a67ca276f8481404cea3398f2c31ed7ee147ebb359d2433a",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.04,
          "end": 4.93,
          "en": "So we get this first basic script here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.93,
          "end": 6.8,
          "en": "which we executed with deno.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 6.8,
          "end": 11.73,
          "en": "Let's now write the same code in our app js file for node.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.73,
          "end": 14.35,
          "en": "So I wanna store some text in a file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.35,
          "end": 16.21,
          "en": "How does this work?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 16.21,
          "end": 17.43,
          "en": "Well first of all,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.43,
          "end": 19.2,
          "en": "I'm setting up my text here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 19.2,
          "end": 21.4,
          "en": "and then in node's world,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 21.4,
          "end": 23.88,
          "en": "I need the file system core module.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 23.88,
          "end": 26.63,
          "en": "We import this with the require syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 26.63,
          "end": 30.87,
          "en": "So from the fs module we import the file system.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.87,
          "end": 32.27,
          "en": "Now here by the way,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 32.27,
          "end": 34.66,
          "en": "I'm getting an error that fs is a module",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 34.66,
          "end": 36.19,
          "en": "that's not being found.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 36.19,
          "end": 37.8,
          "en": "That's of course incorrect.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 37.8,
          "end": 39.97,
          "en": "And for me to fix this to temporarily",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 39.97,
          "end": 43.58,
          "en": "disable my deno extension.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 43.58,
          "end": 44.98,
          "en": "You might not need to do this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 44.98,
          "end": 46.67,
          "en": "I need to do it here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 46.67,
          "end": 49.57,
          "en": "so I will disable it and reload the project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 49.57,
          "end": 51.89,
          "en": "and thereafter this will work here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 51.89,
          "end": 54.11,
          "en": "So now I got the file system here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 54.11,
          "end": 56.32,
          "en": "Now to write to a file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 56.32,
          "end": 59.87,
          "en": "we also got a write file method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 59.87,
          "end": 62.69,
          "en": "the writefile method now also wants",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 62.69,
          "end": 63.99,
          "en": "a path",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 63.99,
          "end": 68.55,
          "en": "which in the simplest form can just be the file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 68.55,
          "end": 71.23,
          "en": "And then it wants the data that should be written.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 71.23,
          "end": 73.73,
          "en": "One core difference compared to deno",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 73.73,
          "end": 76.12,
          "en": "for this specific method here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 76.12,
          "end": 79.34,
          "en": "is that the data could be just a string though,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 79.34,
          "end": 82.44,
          "en": "that we can also pass in such a bytes array,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 82.44,
          "end": 85.63,
          "en": "but that it also just can be a string.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 85.63,
          "end": 87.98,
          "en": "So here we could have to node-message.textfile,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 90.3,
          "end": 94.12,
          "en": "and we just pass in the text as a second argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 94.12,
          "end": 97.53,
          "en": "Now one crucial difference is that write file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 97.53,
          "end": 100.88,
          "en": "like this does now not return a promise,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 100.88,
          "end": 104.35,
          "en": "but that instead we pass in a callback here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 104.35,
          "end": 108.06,
          "en": "to have some code that executes once this completes",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 108.06,
          "end": 110.41,
          "en": "or that tells us about a potential error",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 110.41,
          "end": 112.37,
          "en": "that could have occurred.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 112.37,
          "end": 116.55,
          "en": "However you learn that you can access dot promises here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 116.55,
          "end": 118.89,
          "en": "to then have the promise based versions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 118.89,
          "end": 120.65,
          "en": "of those API is available,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 120.65,
          "end": 123.96,
          "en": "and now write file would give you a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 123.96,
          "end": 127.53,
          "en": "So you can always get a modern feature like a promise here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 127.53,
          "end": 129.89,
          "en": "and to have the best possible comparison",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 129.89,
          "end": 131.21,
          "en": "I'm going to use that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 131.21,
          "end": 132.87,
          "en": "So I'm going to import the file system",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 132.87,
          "end": 136.91,
          "en": "from the promises part of the file system core module,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 136.91,
          "end": 140.32,
          "en": "and therefore now here writefile gives us a promise.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 140.32,
          "end": 141.9,
          "en": "Hence this function will execute",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 141.9,
          "end": 143.87,
          "en": "once writing to a file finished",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 143.87,
          "end": 148.183,
          "en": "and therefore here I can console log wrote file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 149.13,
          "end": 152.06,
          "en": "And now we can save the file and execute it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 152.06,
          "end": 154.51,
          "en": "And for executing it with node,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 154.51,
          "end": 158.63,
          "en": "all we need to do is run node and then the file name.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 158.63,
          "end": 161.32,
          "en": "So the command is just node and the file name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 161.32,
          "end": 165.3,
          "en": "and then that's probably the most striking difference.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 165.3,
          "end": 168.97,
          "en": "We now don't need to specify any permissions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 168.97,
          "end": 172.49,
          "en": "we wanna assign to that execution process.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 172.49,
          "end": 175.4,
          "en": "Instead by default as I mentioned before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 175.4,
          "end": 177.07,
          "en": "node scripts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 177.07,
          "end": 180.32,
          "en": "scripts executed with node by default,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 180.32,
          "end": 182.97,
          "en": "have full read and write access.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 182.97,
          "end": 184.8,
          "en": "They can do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 184.8,
          "end": 187.23,
          "en": "And that of course can be an issue",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 187.23,
          "end": 189.02,
          "en": "because if you're running a script",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 189.02,
          "end": 191.44,
          "en": "from a source which you don't know,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 191.44,
          "end": 194.25,
          "en": "you have to trust that script",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 194.25,
          "end": 197.38,
          "en": "or analyze all the underlying source code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 197.38,
          "end": 201.07,
          "en": "to make sure it's not doing anything harmful",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 201.07,
          "end": 203.47,
          "en": "with denon that's not the case.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 203.47,
          "end": 205.7,
          "en": "There if you execute a script,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 205.7,
          "end": 209.16,
          "en": "you can rely on it only being able to do the things",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 209.16,
          "end": 210.523,
          "en": "you do allow it to do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 211.94,
          "end": 213.37,
          "en": "Of course if you're executing",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 213.37,
          "end": 215.64,
          "en": "some third party script with deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 215.64,
          "end": 217.96,
          "en": "you still might have to scenario that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 217.96,
          "end": 222.29,
          "en": "this script needs write permissions to do what it does",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 222.29,
          "end": 225.06,
          "en": "and well you then again have to trust it",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 225.06,
          "end": 228.02,
          "en": "that it won't abuse those permissions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 228.02,
          "end": 230.38,
          "en": "Anyways, if we now execute this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 230.38,
          "end": 233.4,
          "en": "you see it does finished successfully",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 233.4,
          "end": 237.45,
          "en": "and it writes our message to the node message text file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 237.45,
          "end": 240.87,
          "en": "So this is now the node equivalent of this code,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 240.87,
          "end": 244.5,
          "en": "using some modern node feature here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 244.5,
          "end": 246.98,
          "en": "but otherwise achieving the same result.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 246.98,
          "end": 250.17,
          "en": "So the key difference here really is just typeScript,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 250.17,
          "end": 251.87,
          "en": "which has built into deno,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 251.87,
          "end": 254.453,
          "en": "and of course that permissions thing.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
